      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Usual maximum:** The labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day, given in divided doses of up to about 850 mg to 1,000 mg each. The extended-release maximum is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** The order is about twice the daily maximum. It would raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, split as 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and frequency. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. I'd still recommend checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
